## Backend — tts_server.py (FastAPI, port 8765)

### Dual-mode architecture (laptop + Kaggle GPU)
The laptop server always runs (port 8765). Heavy ML work routes to a **Kaggle GPU
notebook** via cloudflared tunnel when `KAGGLE_ENABLED=true`. When Kaggle is off,
unreachable, or hours are spent, **everything falls back to local CPU** automatically.

| Workload | Kaggle on (`*_PROVIDER=kaggle`) | Local fallback |
|----------|----------------------------------|----------------|
| PDF layout (`/page_layout`) | Kaggle CPU (pdfplumber + PyMuPDF) | `page_layout_service.py` |
| Slide analysis (`/analyze`) | Qwen 3B on GPU (llama-cpp) | Local Qwen via `LLMState` |
| Telugu translation | NLLB-600M on GPU | Local NLLB-1.3B |
| Image upscale | Real-ESRGAN on GPU | Local CPU ESRGAN/Lanczos |
| TTS / karaoke | Always laptop | Sarvam → edge-tts fallback |

Kaggle server: `server/kaggle/veda_gpu_server.py` — endpoints `/health`, `/upload_pdf`,
`/page_layout`, `/analyze`, `/translate`, `/upscale_image`. Tunnel URL changes each
notebook session; update `KAGGLE_API_BASE_URL` in `.env`.

### API Endpoints
| Method | Path | What it does |
|--------|------|--------------|
| GET | /health | Health check + provider modes + Kaggle reachability |
| POST | /upload_pdf | Saves active_doc.pdf; mirrors bytes to Kaggle when layout provider is Kaggle |
| GET | /page_layout?page=N | Returns { width, height, lines[], images[] } — Kaggle or local |
| POST | /analyze | Slide JSON via Kaggle Qwen or local Qwen; Telugu via Kaggle/local NLLB |
| POST | /translate | String list translation — Kaggle or local NLLB, Sarvam fallback |
| POST | /translate_deck | Full deck Telugu — uses `translate_strings_for_deck()` (Kaggle-aware) |
| POST | /translate_fields | Lazy secondary-field translation — Kaggle-aware |
| POST | /tts | Sarvam TTS → returns { audio, word_boundaries[] }; edge-tts fallback |
| GET | /tts_stream | Streams audio (Sarvam or edge-tts fallback) |
| POST | /tts_boundaries | Returns only word_boundaries (no audio) |
| POST | /transcribe | OpenAI Whisper STT → returns { text, word_boundaries[] } |
| POST | /upscale_image | Real-ESRGAN or Lanczos — Kaggle GPU or local CPU |

### Key Classes & Functions
- `SarvamMemoryCache` — in-memory single-entry cache (text+lang+voice+rate as key)
- `LLMState` — singleton for llama-cpp Qwen (local fallback only)
- `IndicTransState` — singleton for NLLB-200-1.3B (local fallback translation)
- `PDFMetadataAnalyzer` — in `page_layout_service.py`; header/footer detection
- `extract_page_layout()` — in `page_layout_service.py`; shared by laptop + Kaggle
- `build_analyze_messages()` / `extract_analysis_json()` — in `analyze_prompts.py`
- `run_semantic_analysis()` — routes `/analyze` to Kaggle or `analyze_text_semantic_local()`
- `translate_strings_for_deck()` — routes all translation to Kaggle or local NLLB
- `kaggle_client` — `should_use_kaggle()`, `kaggle_analyze()`, `kaggle_translate()`,
  `kaggle_page_layout()`, `kaggle_upload_pdf()`, `kaggle_upscale_image()`
- `detect_speech_boundaries(wav_bytes)` — finds lead-in/lead-out silence in WAV
- `adjust_boundaries_to_silence(boundaries, wav_bytes)` — corrects STT timestamps
- `generate_fallback_boundaries(text, duration)` — proportional fallback if STT fails
- `translate_strings_indictrans2()` — local NLLB only (fallback path)
- `translate_strings_sarvam()` — Sarvam Translate API (last-resort fallback)

### LLM Config
- **Primary (when Kaggle on):** Qwen 2.5-3B-Instruct GGUF on Kaggle GPU via llama-cpp (`n_gpu_layers=-1`)
- **Fallback (laptop):** Same model on CPU via `LLMState`
- Model size controlled by env var `LOCAL_LLM_SIZE` (0.5B / 1.5B / 3B) — currently 3B
- Loaded via llama-cpp-python with n_ctx=4096, n_threads=min(8, cpu_count) on laptop
- JSON auto-repair in `analyze_prompts.extract_analysis_json()` (small models produce malformed JSON)
- Auto-downloads GGUF from HuggingFace on first local /analyze if not in server/models/

### Translation (NLLB-200)
- **Kaggle:** facebook/nllb-200-distilled-600M on GPU (env `NLLB_MODEL` on Kaggle server)
- **Laptop fallback:** facebook/nllb-200-1.3B on CPU via `IndicTransState`
- Language code map (INDICTRANS_LANG_MAP): te-IN → tel_Telu, hi-IN → hin_Deva, etc.
- All user-facing translation goes through `translate_strings_for_deck()` (Kaggle-first)
- Sarvam Translate API is last-resort fallback only

### Text + Image Extraction (/page_layout)
- Logic lives in `page_layout_service.extract_page_layout()` — used by laptop and Kaggle
- **Text**: pdfplumber with column detection + image-zone filtering; PyMuPDF fallback
  - Column-aware reading order: gutter ≥ 3% page width → 2-column layout
  - Primary column = more words first; secondary column (sidebar) last
  - Image-zone filtering: words overlapping images by > 30% of word width dropped
  - Header/footer filtering via `PDFMetadataAnalyzer`
- **Images**: PyMuPDF `get_images(full=True)` + `get_image_rects(xref)`
  - Filters: skip w/h < 5, skip w/h < 50 (icons), skip w > 90% page width (backgrounds)
- When `LAYOUT_PROVIDER=kaggle`: PDF mirrored to Kaggle on upload; layout fetched from tunnel

### Known Issues / Things to Watch
1. SarvamMemoryCache is single-entry only — second unique request evicts the first
2. /transcribe uses OpenAI Whisper API (costs money) — Sarvam STT used for karaoke instead
3. CORS is wide open (allow_origins=["*"]) — fine for demo, restrict before production
4. Kaggle tunnel URL (`trycloudflare.com`) changes every notebook restart — update `.env`
5. Kaggle GPU quota: 30 h/week; session must stay open while using Kaggle providers
6. When `KAGGLE_ENABLED=false`, all providers fall back to laptop CPU automatically
7. Laptop still loads local Qwen/NLLB on fallback paths — heavy RAM when Kaggle is off
8. LLMState on laptop is CPU only (no GPU on Windows server)

