## Kaggle GPU Offloading — DONE (Jul 4 2026)
- `server/kaggle/veda_gpu_server.py` — FastAPI on Kaggle T4 x2 + cloudflared tunnel
- Kaggle dataset bundle: Qwen GGUF, RealESRGAN, rrdb_net.py, analyze_prompts.py, page_layout_service.py
- Laptop routes layout/analyze/translate/upscale to Kaggle when enabled; local fallback preserved
- `server/test_kaggle.py --compare` benchmarks local vs Kaggle `/analyze`
- pip package for Kaggle LLM: `llama-cpp-python` (NOT `llama_cpp`) with CUDA wheels
- Keep Sarvam + HeyGen unchanged — TTS stays on laptop (Sarvam primary, edge-tts fallback)

## PDF Layout Improvements — DONE (Jul 3 2026)
- pdfplumber replaces PyMuPDF get_text("dict") for text extraction in /page_layout
- 2-column detection: horizontal gap scan in middle 40% of page, gutter threshold = 3% of page width
- Primary column ordering: column with more words goes first (article body before sidebar)
- Image-zone text filtering: words overlapping images by > 30% of word width are excluded
- Font-size gap clustering for heading detection in detectTopics() (pdfUtils.js)
- Image-primary page handling for cover/ad/photo pages (< 50 words + images)
- Tested against Discovery Nov 2021 (97 pages): 61 single-col, 12 two-col, 14 image-heavy, 10 covers

## Image Upscaling (Real-ESRGAN) — DONE (Jul 2 2026)
- `/upscale_image` POST endpoint in tts_server.py
- `server/rrdb_net.py` — minimal RRDBNet architecture (pure torch, no basicsr dependency)
- Model: RealESRGAN_x4plus.pth (~67MB) in server/models/ — 4× upscale, 23 RRDB blocks
- Tiled inference (256px tiles, 10px pad) keeps peak RAM ~1GB on CPU
- Input images capped at 1024px max side; outputs 4× of capped input
- Frontend: `upscaleImages()` in pdfUtils.js fires concurrently after page layout loads;
  upscaled data-URLs swap into pageDeck.images + topics[*].image once ready (progressive enhancement)
- Dependencies added to server/vendor/: Pillow, opencv-python-headless, torchvision

